The problem involves correcting the wording and punctuation errors to determine the total number of lives. After resolving the issues, the correct question is: "There were 8 friends playing a video game online when 2 more players joined the game. If each player had 6 lives, how many lives did they have total?"

1. Calculate the total number of players after the new players joined:
   $$
   8 \text{ friends} + 2 \text{ players} = 10 \text{ players}
   $$

2. Calculate the total number of lives by multiplying the number of players by the number of lives each player has:
   $$
   10 \text{ players} \times 6 \text{ lives per player} = 60 \text{ lives}
   $$

Thus, the total number of lives is $\boxed{60}$.  
