Frank initially earned $19 from mowing lawns. After spending $11 on new mower blades, the amount of money he has left is calculated by subtracting $11 from $19:

$$
19 - 11 = 8
$$

With the remaining $8, Frank wants to buy games that cost $2 each. To find out how many games he can buy, we divide the remaining money by the cost of each game:

$$
8 \div 2 = 4
$$

Thus, the number of $2 games Frank can buy with the money he has left is $\boxed{4}$. 
