So yes, 65 total, subtract 17 not picked, gives 48. Divided into 8 groups, so 48 divided by 8 is 6. 

Another way to think about it: if you have 8 groups and you want to split 48 students equally, each group would have 6. That seems right. 

I don't think there's any trick here. The problem is straightforward. Maybe there's a possibility that the 17 didn't get picked, but the rest were put into groups. So the rest is 65-17=48. Then 48 divided by 8 is 6. Yep. 

