First, the total number of students is 65. Then, 17 didn't get picked for the team, so we need to subtract those from the total to find out how many were put into groups.

65 total students - 17 who didn't get picked = 48 students who were put into groups.

Now, these 48 students are divided into 8 groups. To find out how many students are in each group, we divide 48 by 8.

48 ÷ 8 = 6

So, each group would have 6 students. 

