Hmm, so both methods give me 30. So, I think the answer is 30. I don't see any other factors here. The problem doesn't mention any exceptions or different numbers of problems per page for different subjects. It just says each page has 5 problems. So, 2 + 4 = 6 pages total. 6 * 5 = 30. Yep, that's straightforward.

