First, I need to find out how much total money Jerry has. So he made 14 from mowing and 31 from weed eating. Let me add those two amounts together. 14 plus 31... Hmm, 14 + 30 is 44, and then plus 1 more is 45. So total money is 45 dollars.

Now, he spends 5 dollars each week. The question is asking how long his money will last. So I need to divide his total money by the amount he spends each week. That is, 45 divided by 5. Let me do that division. 5 times 9 is 45, so 45 divided by 5 is 9. So it would last him 9 weeks.

Wait, but let me check again. Maybe I missed something? The problem mentions "how long would the money last him?" So if he spends 5 dollars per week, then each week he uses up 5 dollars. So with 45 dollars, he can do 45 divided by 5. Yeah, that's 9 weeks. That seems right. 

