The problem states that Will earns $8 per hour at a grocery store. On Monday, he worked 8 hours, and on Tuesday, he worked 2 hours. To find the total earnings, we calculate the earnings for each day and sum them.

**Monday's earnings:**
$$
8 \, \text{hours} \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 64 \, \text{dollars}
$$

**Tuesday's earnings:**
$$
2 \, \text{hours} \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 16 \, \text{dollars}
$$

**Total earnings:**
$$
64 \, \text{dollars} + 16 \, \text{dollars} = 80 \, \text{dollars}
$$

Thus, the total amount of money Will made in those two days is $\boxed{80}$. 
